<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mohammed el-Kebir</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1797">1797</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mohammed el-Kebir was bey of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">Beylik</a> of the West, the western province of the Regency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>, from 1779 to 1797. He besieged Spanish-held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> and took possession of it in 1792, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> agreed to leave following the earthquake of 1790, and made it his capital. He built mosques and other works in the city and extended Algerian authority over the western tribes.</p></div>
